1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,706
From lesson observation to a plan for every teacher.

2
00:00:05,706 --> 00:00:10,692
Here is what the system does today, and where staff voice fits into it.

3
00:00:12,692 --> 00:00:14,315
From there, four steps.

4
00:00:14,315 --> 00:00:15,937
The observation is filed.

5
00:00:15,937 --> 00:00:17,560
The teacher gets feedback.

6
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:24,050
The Teacher Coach receives an analysis and a suggested coaching plan to approve, edit, or rewrite.

7
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:30,541
And the teacher receives that plan, every suggestion referenced back to our own Student Progress Rubric.

8
00:00:30,891 --> 00:00:33,376
This is what the Teacher Coach receives.

9
00:00:33,376 --> 00:00:37,636
This teacher is Acceptable on progress in lessons; the plan targets Good.

10
00:00:37,636 --> 00:00:45,091
The rubric line for that level, one concrete move, what to look for next lesson, and where the technique comes from.

11
00:00:45,091 --> 00:00:49,351
The Teacher Coach approves, edits, swaps the strategy, or writes their own.

12
00:00:49,701 --> 00:00:52,486
What the loop does not hear yet is the teacher.

13
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:54,836
We capture how a session was rated.

14
00:00:54,836 --> 00:01:03,992
We do not capture what the teacher made of it, what they expect to struggle with when they apply it, or what they will actually do differently on Monday morning.

15
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:07,920
So, the first addition.

16
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,775
An evaluation of the professional learning session itself.

17
00:01:10,775 --> 00:01:19,342
Short, completed by the teacher, in place before the coaching plan is drafted, so the Teacher Coach and the analysis both see it first.

18
00:01:19,692 --> 00:01:20,618
The second addition.

19
00:01:20,618 --> 00:01:23,087
A reflection and an action plan, six things.

20
00:01:23,087 --> 00:01:25,248
What the teacher took from the session.

21
00:01:25,248 --> 00:01:27,409
The challenges they expect in applying it.

22
00:01:27,409 --> 00:01:29,569
Their own ideas for getting past those.

23
00:01:29,569 --> 00:01:32,038
How they will use it in their classroom.

24
00:01:32,038 --> 00:01:34,199
What they need from their line manager.

25
00:01:34,199 --> 00:01:37,903
And what they expect to change in student learning, over what timeframe.

26
00:01:38,253 --> 00:01:46,624
Today, the analysis reads the Teacher Coach's own notes, finds where the teacher sits on the rubric, and grounds every recommendation in trusted published sources.

27
00:01:46,624 --> 00:01:59,349
Next, our own shelf: line managers and heads of department write five coachable Teaching Strategies for every point of the rubric, and the system recommends the one that fits the level above, straight from the teacher's own evidence.

28
00:01:59,699 --> 00:02:05,026
On top of that shelf, Claire Gadsby's Teacher Strategies, one for every point of the rubric.

29
00:02:05,026 --> 00:02:12,683
For example: where questioning reaches only student volunteers within a lesson, the plan automatically recommends a Teacher Strategy focused on Class Response Boards.

30
00:02:12,683 --> 00:02:14,015
One on every desk.

31
00:02:14,015 --> 00:02:17,011
The teacher asks, answers up on one, two, three.

32
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:22,671
Every pupil's answer visible in eight seconds, allowing a concept reteach on the spot, not next week.

33
00:02:23,021 --> 00:02:27,316
A second Teacher Strategy centres on student engagement: pupils take ownership of the unit.

34
00:02:27,316 --> 00:02:28,543
The Pupil Owned Corner.

35
00:02:28,543 --> 00:02:35,292
One marked square metre, curated by a rotating pair for a fortnight: an artefact, a clipping, a question they cannot answer yet.

36
00:02:35,292 --> 00:02:41,428
Sixty seconds at the start of one lesson, and the next five minutes of teaching build on what they said.

37
00:02:43,928 --> 00:02:47,442
Staff responses then get the same treatment as the observation data.

38
00:02:47,442 --> 00:02:50,317
Themes across the school, not a folder of replies.

39
00:02:50,317 --> 00:02:51,915
Where support is asked for.

40
00:02:51,915 --> 00:02:53,512
Which challenges repeat, and where.

41
00:02:53,512 --> 00:02:57,026
All of it carrying references, exactly as the observation claims do.

42
00:02:57,376 --> 00:02:59,819
Line managers see their own team, and nobody else's.

43
00:02:59,819 --> 00:03:02,391
This is not another report to read through.

44
00:03:02,391 --> 00:03:08,891
It is a starting point for a real coaching conversation, with the teacher's own words already sitting in front of them.

45
00:03:09,241 --> 00:03:11,587
Which gives every teacher a plan of their own.

46
00:03:11,587 --> 00:03:16,398
Built from their lesson, from their own words, and from their answers to both forms.

47
00:03:16,398 --> 00:03:18,934
Ready and waiting on their own Teacher Portal.

48
00:03:19,284 --> 00:03:22,076
The two forms are new; the architecture is not.

49
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:27,349
Same intake, same evidence rules, same dashboard, same privacy layer, the data staying in our own database.

50
00:03:27,349 --> 00:03:29,831
Student surveys run on the same rails next.
